\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{An odd period changes the filtered degree}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Refine the circle of period #{3} to period #{6}. At common dimensionless mass #{\mu=5/2} the vertex [bulk integer](fdip-019W) on the coarse circle is #{1} from its origin. The fine circle also has a sampled #{\pi} of degree #{-1} and mass #{2<\mu}, so its vertex integer is zero.}

\p{At #{\mu=7/4}, include the off-vertex centered zero in the coarse filtered count. By \ref{fdip-01BX} its interpolated mass at #{\pi} is #{1+\cos(\pi /3)=3/2}; the fine mass there is #{2}. The signed counts of all interpolated zeros below #{\mu} are consequently #{1-1=0} and #{1}. Both cutoffs avoid the actual thresholds.}
